            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0343" n="229" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-09T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 9—4:47
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>430. Your instruction number 879, July 18th.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d154-f1"/> The
                    Admiralty will give Major Davidson, our air attaché here, all information
                    desired. The Air Ministry is expected to take the same attitude.</p>
                <p>Canada will assist the pathfinding officers in every way. There is no objection
                    to their Canadian itinerary as outlined in the above named instruction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harvey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
